Cell["5.  Decision boundary as a tropical hypersurface", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d95aacd1-d4b7-4971-85e2-49e49f087a27"],

Cell["\<\
The hidden units cut the input plane along n straight lines a_j . x + b_j = 0 \
(the ReLU 'creases'). On each open region of the resulting arrangement, the \
activation pattern sigma in {0, 1}^n is constant, and f is affine. The \
decision boundary {f = 0} is a piecewise-linear curve that snaps to the \
crease arrangement - it is the tropical hypersurface {P = Q}.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9fb63eb1-ce03-42a1-bd5a-d6bb6eae71c5"],

