Cell["6.  Newton polytope of a tropical polynomial", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0d0adda6-16d8-40b9-adac-a88c28f11fe5"],

Cell["\<\
Every tropical polynomial P(x) = max_i (a_i . x + c_i) has a Newton polytope \
Newt(P) = conv{a_i}, and the upper convex hull of {(a_i, c_i)} in R^3 induces \
a regular subdivision of Newt(P). That subdivision is dual to the \
linear-region decomposition of input space induced by P. Monomials whose \
lifted point lies in the interior of the upper envelope are dominated by \
other terms and never realise the max - they contribute no region.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6af72392-8b1c-4cc2-af3e-527992cf8d6d"],

