Cell["7.  Linear regions scale like n^2", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e1ba10f1-2417-4d11-bb6f-958d7644795b"],

Cell["\<\
n lines in general position in R^2 partition the plane into at most Z(n) = 1 \
+ n + C(n, 2) open regions (Zaslavsky). Training a 2 -> n -> 1 ReLU \
classifier and counting distinct activation patterns on a fine grid gives the \
empirical scaling below. The trained network sits at ~0.5-0.95 of the bound \
and matches its asymptotic slope exactly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3f62724-e76c-4485-be4f-dce90ecae58f"],

